(c4) TAn[Down in adoration falling This great Sacrament we hail; Ancient](e)tum(e) er(f)go(ed) sa(g)cra(g)mén(hj)tum(j) *(,) ve(jk)ne(j)ré(j)mur(i) cér(h)nu(j)i,(ivHG) (:) 
 et(g) an[types have long departed, Newer rites of grace prevail, Faith for all defects](h)tí(j)quum(i) do(h)cu(g)mén(h)tum(g) (,) no(h)vo(i) ce(g)dat(g) rí(e)tu(h)i;(hd) (:) 
 præ(e)stet(g) fi(g)des(e) sup(g)ple[supplying, Where the feeble senses fail. Glory, let us give, and blessing To the ](h)mén(h)tum(g) (,) sen(h)su(i)um(g) de(hg)féc(fe)tu(d)i.(e) (::)
Ge(e)ni(e)tó(f)ri(ed) Ge(g)ni(g)tó(hj)que(j) (,) laus(jk) et(j) ju[Father and the Son. Honour, might and praise addressing, While eternal ages run.](j)bi(i)lá(h)ti(j)o,(ivHG) (:) 
 sa(g)lus,(h) ho(j)nor,(i) vir(h)tus(g) quo(h)que(g) (,) sit(h) et(i) be(g)ne(g)díc(e)ti(h)o;[/](hd) (:) 
 Pro[Equal praise to Him confessing, Who proceeds from both as one.](e)ce(g)dén(g)ti(e) ab(g) u(h)tró(h)que(g) (,) com(h)par(i) sit(g) lau(hg)dá(fe)ti(d)o.(e) (::) A(efe)men.(de) (::)
